  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Improving conditions today with noticeable \nwarmup to end September and start October \n\nDreary start today with widespread low clouds and patchy \nfog/drizzle. Expect gradual improvement today with more clouds\nthan sun and max temps +5-10 degrees warmer vs. Monday in the\n65-75F range. \n\nMore breaks in the clouds overnight will favor locally dense\nvalley fog formation with very low visibility restrictions into\nearly Wednesday morning. \n\nSizable warmup expected from mid to late week with fcst max \ntemps in the 75-85F range or +10-15 degrees above the historical\naverage for the end of September/beginning of October. For \ncontext, the average last date of max temp >=80F is 9/27 at \nState College, 9/29 at Altoona, 10/2 at Williamsport and 10/5 at\nHarrisburg. \n\nNo rainfall is forecast through Thursday with some showers\npossible on Friday-Friday night associated with cold front\nsinking southeastward from the eastern Great Lakes.  \n---------------------------------------------------------------\n \nKEY MESSAGE 2: Cooling trend this weekend into early next week \nwith an increasing chance of rain Saturday and Sunday \n\n24hr maxT change on Saturday behind the cold front is fcst to \nbe 10-15 degrees lower vs. Friday with highs in the low 60s/70s.\nTrailing frontal wave could bring more widespread soaking rain\non Sunday based on WPC/NBM QPF - although EC/CMC and (to lesser\nextent) lean farther to the south/east with the frontal precip.\nConfidence is higher that temps continue to cool off and drop \nnear or below the historical average into early next week. Frost\npotential is on the table for next Monday and Tuesday night.",
